From 429027982927046dfb8631cec3da837020b14835 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:20:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] patches/openwrt: fix powerpc32 eBPF JIT miscompilations

The powerpc32 eBPF JIT used by mpc85xx and apm821xx miscompiles
BPF-to-BPF calls (wrong halves of the first argument and the return
value, missing fifth argument) and loses the lower half of a register
when a 32-bit MOV is followed by the verifier's zero-extension. Clang
emits the latter when chaining bpf_csum_diff() calls, so CLAT sent
packets with bad L4 checksums with bpf_jit_enable=1.

Carry the pending series by Lukas Stockner until it is upstream.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
