+From 0aaf7b99afdbd06a53e04a0b1eed1bfbe207d938 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
+Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:20:13 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH] kernel: fix powerpc32 eBPF JIT miscompilations
+
+The powerpc32 eBPF JIT, used by mpc85xx and apm821xx, passes the wrong
+halves of the first argument and of the return value in BPF-to-BPF
+calls, drops the fifth argument of subprograms, and loses the lower
+half of a register when a 32-bit MOV is followed by the verifier's
+zero-extension. Clang emits the latter when chaining bpf_csum_diff()
+calls, so CLAT sent packets with bad L4 checksums with bpf_jit_enable=1.
+
+Add the pending series by Lukas Stockner, which also brings kfunc call
+code for the 32-bit JIT and a bpf_kptr_xchg() fix for 32-bit big-endian.
+Two commits are adapted to 6.6, which has no ctx->is_subprog and no
+separate fimage.
+
+Link: https://github.com/lukasstockner/linux/tree/ppc32-ebpf-jit-fixes
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
